This paper is a solid method contribution with a mathematically clean framework and compelling empirical results, but its scope is limited (2 architectures, 2 training modifications) and some claims lack statistical backing. It is stronger than the low-scoring anchors but weaker than the high-scoring accepted methods papers in terms of breadth of evaluation. It lands in the borderline-to-weak-accept range, similar to SIMPL and the Neural ODE Transformers paper.

